00:23:24.880 --> 00:23:25.960
Make AD equal.

00:23:25.960 --> 00:23:30.246
DE have been drawn through point D parallel to ...

00:23:30.354 --> 00:23:30.840
31.

00:23:30.840 --> 00:23:33.720
Draw a straight line parallel to a given straight line through a given.

00:23:33.880 --> 00:23:35.080
Gonna have me make alternate.

00:23:35.080 --> 00:23:38.579
Let angle DAE equal to angle ADC have been constructed

00:23:38.579 --> 00:23:41.170
on the straight line DA proposition 23.

00:23:42.050 --> 00:23:43.450
Back to proposition 46.

00:23:43.450 --> 00:23:46.250
Let DE have been drawn through point D parallel to AD.

00:23:46.250 --> 00:23:49.330
And let BE have been drawn through point B parallel to AD.

00:23:49.410 --> 00:23:52.290
This and this are parallel, and this and this are also parallel.

00:23:52.290 --> 00:23:53.249
And this angle is equal to.

00:23:53.249 --> 00:23:56.290
Thus we have a square with four equal sides and four right angles.

00:23:58.850 --> 00:24:02.796
The key steps here were that after drawing the second side so that it was

00:24:02.796 --> 00:24:05.391
perpendicular and equal in length to the first,

00:24:05.391 --> 00:24:08.635
the third side was constructed to be parallel to the first,

00:24:08.635 --> 00:24:11.230
and the fourth side was parallel to the second.

00:24:11.630 --> 00:24:16.350
This allows him to then use the already established properties of parallelograms to

00:24:16.350 --> 00:24:21.070
state that the opposite sides and the opposite angles are all equal to each other.

00:24:21.790 --> 00:24:24.258
With my simpler method of constructing the square,

00:24:24.258 --> 00:24:28.206
I wouldn't have been able to prove that it was a square at all without invoking

00:24:28.206 --> 00:24:29.390
the parallel postulate.

00:24:29.550 --> 00:24:34.732
But it's actually even worse than that, because without the parallel postulate,

00:24:34.732 --> 00:24:36.110
