You know, to do it algebraically, to take algebras to fundamental foundation,

00:31:26.562 --> 00:31:29.320
is he's the one who shows that that could easily be done.

00:31:29.480 --> 00:31:30.920
And still he refuses.

00:31:31.000 --> 00:31:34.476
He has the standing at the gates of paradise where he's denying himself,

00:31:34.476 --> 00:31:36.600
you know, saying, no, no, no, that's wrong.

00:31:36.680 --> 00:31:37.800
We should do it this way.

00:31:37.800 --> 00:31:40.920
He insists on this classical stuff eat despite himself.

00:31:40.920 --> 00:31:43.878
But soon the reign of constructions as the philosophical

00:31:43.878 --> 00:31:46.360
bedrock for math would have to come to an end.

00:31:46.520 --> 00:31:50.940
The 19th century realization that there are valid forms of geometry where

00:31:50.940 --> 00:31:55.421
the parallel postulate is false, along with other seemingly contradictory

00:31:55.421 --> 00:31:59.780
discoveries in that century, led to a sear formal foundations for math.

00:32:00.180 --> 00:32:05.620
Math increasingly turned to formal logic, which today is embodied by computer systems.

00:32:06.340 --> 00:32:09.013
Rather than relying on intuition or abstract thought,

00:32:09.013 --> 00:32:12.292
computerized proof checkers like Lean serve a similar purpose to

00:32:12.292 --> 00:32:16.580
the one that a skeptic with a ruler and compass would have served in ancient Greece.

00:32:17.860 --> 00:32:22.216
Just like in those early days of axiomatic deductive mathematics,

00:32:22.216 --> 00:32:28.180
we still need tools that ground abstract reasoning in systematic, verifiable procedures.

00:32:29.140 --> 00:32:30.500
Instead of constructions,

00:32:30.580 --> 00:32:34.774
Computer systems are built on countless on off switches of transistors,

00:32:34.774 --> 00:32:36.900
following explicit checkable rules.

00:32:38.340 --> 00:32:42.632
As is the case with Euclid, smaller operations based on fundamental starting

00:32:42.632 --> 00:32:46.980
points form subroutines that build into ever larger programmatic structures.

00:32:47.700 --> 00:32:55.150
But where Euclid's basic operations were lines and circles, ours are ones and zeros.

00:32:57.390 --> 00:33:00.920
There was a very strong parallel between understanding what Euclid was

00:33:00.920 --> 00:33:04.602
really getting at with constructions, and like my own process for making

00:33:04.602 --> 00:33:08.536
videos with programmatic animation, that which felt like a very modern thing,

00:33:08.536 --> 00:33:11.966
like wanting to implement it on a computer, was actually maybe more

00:33:11.966 --> 00:33:15.950
reflective of how people's relationship was with math through most of history.

00:33:16.190 --> 00:33:16.910
I don't have...

00:33:16.910 --> 00:33:20.892
I'm not a computer coder, but there are many similar ways where actually

00:33:20.892 --> 00:33:25.040
having to instantiate something changes it from what you had in your mind.

00:33:25.040 --> 00:33:27.560
And I did find that kind of core idea.

